  ('a87a6822-48c7-54e2-a0d4-d1ae90b4d3e0', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read: "When glaciers on land melt, the water flows into the ocean and raises sea levels. ____, floating sea ice that melts has little effect on sea level, because it was already displacing water before it melted." Which transition best completes the sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By contrast,","is_correct":true},{"text":"Similarly,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comparison-for-contrast"},{"text":"Consequently,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contrast-for-effect"},{"text":"For instance,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-for-contrast"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By contrast,$q$, $q$The two sentences describe opposite outcomes, one kind of melting raises sea level and the other does not, so "By contrast" fits. "Similarly" is wrong because the second sentence describes a different result, not a parallel one.$q$, 'draft', null)
