  ('d7b2fbb7-cad0-5840-a042-a445c6a13929', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read: "A survey found that students who kept a written study schedule reported less stress before exams. ____, the survey cannot show that the schedules caused the lower stress; students who were already calm may simply have been more likely to keep schedules." Which transition best completes the sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"However,","is_correct":true},{"text":"Therefore,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"qualification-read-as-effect"},{"text":"Specifically,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-for-qualification"},{"text":"In fact,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"intensifier-for-qualification"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$However,$q$, $q$The second sentence limits the conclusion a reader might draw from the first, so the contrasting "However" fits. "In fact" is tempting because it often follows a finding, but it would wrongly signal that the second sentence strengthens the first rather than qualifying it.$q$, 'draft', null)
