  ('7ef076ec-1a2c-5030-985c-a7515e8852e4', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the paragraph: "(1) Magnetic levitation trains float above their guideways rather than rolling on wheels. (2) Powerful magnets lift each car a short distance off the track and propel it forward. (3) Because nothing touches the rails, there is almost no friction to slow the train. (4) Tickets for long-distance trains are often cheaper when booked several weeks in advance. (5) This lack of friction allows the trains to reach very high speeds while running quietly." Which sentence should be removed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 4","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 2","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Sentence 5","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-concluding-sentence"},{"text":"Sentence 3","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 4$q$, $q$The paragraph explains how levitation reduces friction and increases speed, and ticket prices have nothing to do with that explanation. Sentence 5 should stay because "This lack of friction" connects back to sentence 3 and completes the reasoning.$q$, 'draft', null)
