   $q$Read: "Thick earthen walls have kept desert homes comfortable for centuries. ____, the walls absorb the sun's heat slowly during the day and release it at night, when the air outside turns cold." Which transition best completes the sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Specifically,","is_correct":true},{"text":"Instead,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"replacement-for-explanation"},{"text":"Even so,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"concession-for-explanation"},{"text":"Previously,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"time-for-explanation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Specifically,$q$, $q$The second sentence explains in detail how the walls keep homes comfortable, so "Specifically" signals a closer look at the first sentence's claim. "Even so" is wrong because the second sentence supports the first instead of conceding a point against it.$q$, 'draft', null)
