  ('970f5a75-1696-5c21-a467-d55de8e9e68c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In which sentence does the transition express a relationship that does not fit the ideas it connects?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The exhibit drew record crowds; nevertheless, the gift shop sold out of its catalog within a week.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The museum extended its weekend hours; consequently, attendance on Sundays rose by nearly a third.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-cause-effect"},{"text":"The curators expected little interest in the textile collection; however, it became the season's most visited gallery.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-contrast"},{"text":"The archive's oldest maps are too fragile to handle; therefore, visitors view high-resolution scans instead.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The exhibit drew record crowds; nevertheless, the gift shop sold out of its catalog within a week.$q$, $q$Record crowds and a sold-out catalog fit together, so "nevertheless," which signals an unexpected contrast, is illogical there. The textile sentence correctly uses "however" because the gallery's popularity went against the curators' expectations.$q$, 'draft', null)
